This extension adds The Last of Us Part I modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Automatically installs UnPSARC.[/summary]

[b][color=#b6d7a8]This extension will automatically download and install [url=https://github.com/rm-NoobInCoding/UnPSARC]UnPSARC[/url].  You can use this tool to extract the vanilla .psarc game files.[/color] [size=3][color=#ea9999]YOU MUST DO THIS STEP FOR DATA MODS TO WORK! [/color][color=#b6d7a8]You will receive a Vortex notification where you can do the extraction.[/color][/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Build Folder mods with a "build" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Bin Folder mods with a "bin" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file install to the "build\pc\main" folder.[/*]
[*]Pak (actor97) mods with a ".pak" file install to the "build\pc\main" folder.[/*]
[*]Build Folder mods with a "build" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Save mods with a "USR-DATA" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\The Last of Us Part I\users\<User ID>\savedata" folder.[/*]
[*]Config mods with a "screeninfo.cfg" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\The Last of Us Part I\users\<User ID>" folder.[/*]
[*]UnPSARC Tool mods with a "UnPSARC.exe" file install to the "build\pc\main" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]You must run the extraction function to get the data out of the vanilla .psarc files and rename them. Purging mods will revert these changes.[/*]
[*]You can execute and reverse the game file extraction process, as well as open other files/folders/URLs, using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods page toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for The Last of Us Part I mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Build Folder Pak Bin:

Recognised when the archive contains a "build" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

bin Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "bin" folder, a ".pak" file and a ".bin" file.

  Installs to: "build\pc\main"

========================================================================

Pak (actor97):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".pak" file.

  Installs to: "build\pc\main"

========================================================================

Build Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "build" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "USR-DATA".

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\The Last of Us Part I\users\<User ID>\savedata"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Configuration tweaks, deployed to the game's config location.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "screeninfo.cfg".

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Saved Games\The Last of Us Part I\users\<User ID>"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod makes the whole archive install as a config mod.

========================================================================

UnPSARC Tool:

Recognised when the archive contains a "UnPSARC.exe" file.

  Installs to: "build\pc\main"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

